  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Carbohydrate molecules have hemiacetal or hemiketal groups can reduces Tollen&#39;s reagent and Fehling&#39;s solution are reducing. All monosaccharides are reducing sugars. If any sugar is having free <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>OH</mi></math> group at anomeric carbon then it will be a reducing sugar.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ec6aded6-a004-4c29-8a48-32d590657952-60bd1f5f-51d2-40ee-8d79-0c4553a79072-image.png\" style=\"width: 416px; height: 240px;\" /></p></blockquote>",
